Line-by-line reading:
- `label "harness-failed" already exists — nothing to create` — **`ensureHarnessFailedLabel`'s
  already-exists classifier fired correctly at startup.** This is the arm whose
  dead-code regex was the T2 blocking defect (`69fddac` → fixed at `5470a97`):
  before that fix, gh's stderr never reached the thrown error under
  `stdio: "inherit"`, so this branch was unreachable and this very run would
  have **aborted pre-spend**. This is the first live proof of that fix.
- `https://github.com/manjula25/loop-fixtures-py/issues/54#issuecomment-5794216701`
  — the FR-002 escalation comment, posted inline the moment the lane failed.
- `https://github.com/manjula25/loop-fixtures-py/issues/54` — the FR-004
  `--add-label harness-failed` edit, whose output is the issue URL.
- `Loop finished without a PR — Fix run produced no commits — nothing to verify
  or PR.` — the `formatSingleIssueResult` line. **The `Reason:` line in the
  posted comment is byte-identical to this string** (FR-002).
- `RUN2-EXIT: 1` (run 1 exited 0 — the exit code distinguishes the two).

