## Run 3 — plan step 4: the label-removal half (issue #54 made fixable)

Authorized separately (the two-run budget was consumed; run 1 was wasted on the
invalid seed). The **same issue #54** was amended — body replaced with a plainly
fixable requirement — so that it *kept* its `harness-failed` label and its
escalation comment. That is the plan's "amend the issue to something fixable"
route, and it is the only way to witness a real removal: the label must be
present when a verified PR is delivered.

Amendment: `word_count` must not count whitespace-separated chunks with no
alphanumeric character — `word_count("hello --- world") == 2` — with every other
behaviour unchanged. Verified to be a **real** defect first (pre-fix:
`word_count("hello --- world")` → `3`), so the RED is genuine, not staged.

Post-amend, pre-run state:
`{"number":54,"state":"OPEN","labels":["harness-failed"],"comments":1}` — the
label survived the body edit, and the run-2 escalation comment was still there.

