### T5 conclusion

Every element the plan's T5 set out to prove is now witnessed live against real
`gh` and a real Docker sandbox: the escalation comment (content, handle arm,
outcome class, byte-identical reason, single post, no retry), the label add, the
label remove on delivered success, the failed lane leaving no PR and no branch,
and — unplanned but valuable — `ensureHarnessFailedLabel`'s already-exists
classifier, which is the T2 blocking-defect arm.

**Non-claims:** A9 (a *genuine* gh error during a label remove being swallowed by
the broad `not found` classifier) is **not** exercised by any of these runs and
remains open as recorded; the runs only exercised the intended idempotent-absent
branch. The preflight-failed and reverted/uncanaried arms were not produced live.
The absent-handle (`notify handle not configured`) arm was not produced live —
the fixtures profile sets a handle, so only the present arm was witnessed; the
absent arm stays vitest-only.